 "honesty": {
  "control_fixture_correction": "the first run of test_stage07_controls.py failed 4 of 25 controls, including the positive control. Root cause was the synthetic fixture, not the engine: it set q(last)=4 while chainFactors anchors factor=1 on the last date. The real cohort was then measured and satisfies q(last)==1 on 30/30 symbols. The fixture was corrected to a real 2:1 split with a flat type7 series, and control G was added to prove an anchor violation is detected. No engine, tolerance or acceptance criterion changed.",
  "gate_correction_disclosure": "the first run of this stage gated adjusted_candles rows on all 30 symbols and reported PARTIAL. That expectation was wrong: the builder only materializes symbols carrying factor rows. The gate was corrected to the builder's actual scope and a Runtime measurement of the zero-event symbol was added in stage08. No Phase 4.9.2 acceptance criterion or tolerance was changed, and no failing check was deleted.",
  "no_second_engine": "factors come from Phase 4.9.2's own q_changes/classify and candles from the shipped Go candlebuild; nothing was rewritten",
  "ohlc_widening": "open/high/low differences are reported separately from close. Every high/low difference is attributed to the frozen widen contract acting on a source bar whose open lies outside its own high/low; an unattributed difference fails the stage. Neither the raw bars nor the engine were modified.",
  "substrate_difference": "Phase 4.9.2 measured on a Seed copy; this runs on a fresh schema-only DB. Candle-level acceptance is comparable because the engine reads only the three reference tables, but the Seed-dependent measurements are listed as NOT_MEASURED",
  "tolerance_unchanged": "the engine's 1e-9 EXACT threshold and the frozen pack windows are used as-is; no tolerance was relaxed to make this green",
  "unclassified_is_not_guessed": "an event with no official witness stays corporate_action_unclassified; its type is never inferred from the ratio"
 },
